{
  "_comment": [
    "Differential corpus for the eight built-in assertions (spec 003).",
    "`fixtures` is the file tree both halves build before running; a value of",
    "null means 'a directory' and a value of '@hex:...' means those raw bytes.",
    "`@FX` in any case string is the fixture root,",
    "substituted in before the case runs and substituted back out of the",
    "recorded detail, so an absolute path is comparable across machines.",
    "Case defaults: cwd '@FX', screen 'SCREEN text', raw_output 'RAW output',",
    "exit_code 0, kind 'assertion'."
  ],
  "fixtures": {
    "exists.txt": "hello fixture\nsecond line\n",
    "empty.txt": "",
    "utf8.txt": "café ☕\n",
    "latin1.bin": "@hex:61ff62",
    "realsub": null,
    "realsub/keep.txt": "nested\n",
    "schema-object.json": "{\"type\": \"object\"}",
    "schema-string.json": "{\"type\": \"string\"}",
    "schema-bad-json.json": "{'a': 1}",
    "schema-invalid.json": "{\"type\": \"nope\"}"
  },
  "cases": [
